  "changelog": [
    {
      "item": "S9.0-1 +5V removed",
      "change": "The module is +/-12V only: U3 (TPS62933F +5V buck) and every part that only served +5V are gone (U23 eFuse with R108/TP21, OVLO R107/R101/R102, ILM R103/R104, dVdt C68, L2 and the U3 network, the raw and delivered +5V banks, D3/D21/D23, the U20 +5V guard channel, the U18 +5V monitor, R44, TP13/TP18, J2/J3 pins 11/12 open). No +5V/P5_*/EF_* net or ref survives (regression tests)."
    },
    {
      "item": "S9.0-2 15 V input",
      "change": "CH224A requests 15 V (R1 56k); U5 UVLO R3 10k (on 12.46-13.98 V, off 11.55-13.13 V); V20_OK R83 100k (7.67-9.27 V status floor); stated input range 13.5-16.5 V at the module; needs a 15 V / 3 A (>= 45 W) PD source; U5 OVP keeps the 20 V setting."
    },
    {
      "item": "S9.0-2 +12V duty",
      "change": "The S8 TPS62933F buck needed 0.995-1.053 duty at the 12.5 V low-line converter input (1.033 even unloaded at the setpoint maximum) against its 98 % maximum and would need VPD >= 14.42 V: replaced by the TPS552892-Q1 four-switch buck-boost (TI RYQ0021B; 966 kHz, L1 6.8 uH kept, R109 15 mR CC limit 3.14-3.53 A, FB R8/R9, COMP R111/C83, VCC C82, FPWM, internal LDO) that regulates from the 10.55 V U5 sag to 21 V. U2 footprint replaced (U2 only), +10 parts placed right of L1."
    },
    {
      "item": "S9.0 ratings",
      "change": "Published prototype rating +12V 2.4 A, -12V 0.8 A (75 % of the minimum current-limited capability at the 12.5 V converter input), <= 33 W together (3 A contract at the 13.5 V minimum, worst efficiency mix); ~36 W is the most a nominal 15 V / 3 A source supports."
    },
    {
      "item": "S9.0 arming",
      "change": "Re-derived without P5_OK: ANY_BAD = NAND(MAIN_LED_OK, P12_OK, N12_OK, V3V3); S8.5 one-shot STARTED (U12 A, U11 -> ARMED, TP19) kept; timelines re-run at the 15 V source corners with a load-aware VPD plant (the loaded 13.5 V minimum sits below the 13.98 V turn-on maximum): 0 violations."
    },
    {
      "item": "S9.0 residuals",
      "change": "Owner decisions 2026-11-02: no reverse-current blocking (no LM74700/LTC4357-class part, no FETs) and no voltage-triggered fuse/crowbar; both recorded as accepted residuals with bench-test conditions and pass criteria (calcs residuals, validation accepted_residuals, docs S9.0). Finding: a live +/-12V bus can enable U4 through Q1 in an unpowered module and its FPWM can pump VIN: the procedural rule is mandatory; a non-blocking mitigation is an open owner decision, not implemented."
    },
    {
      "item": "kept / open",
      "change": "Crowbar vs eFuse stays deferred/open (no crowbar restored); replug/POR race (C3) open; U18/U20 on VPD, guard thresholds, precision-divider policy, mechanics and the panel geometry unchanged (panel label PD 15V)."
    }
  ],
