    "arming_calcs": {
      "required": [
        "R1 bounded: ARMED within the U11 delay (0.31-0.88 s) of the first converter enable after RESET, and held until RESET/FAULT: the converters can never run unarmed for longer",
        "R2 no restart: nothing a fault can toggle (MAIN_OK, PGOOD, VPD, V20_OK, the rails) restarts or extends the window; only RESET (or a power-on reset) does",
        "R3 no early arming: the window starts only at a genuine converter enable, i.e. U5 on through its own UVLO with valid status; the PD 5 V phase or an intermediate PDO cannot start it, so no threshold below the converter enable point can arm",
        "R4 fail-safe: after ARMED any bad status > ~1 ms latches FAULT; FAULT holds RUN low until RESET; OV_N (U20 guard: +12V and -12V channels) presets FAULT at any time"
      ],
      "topology": {
        "STARTED": "U12 flip-flop A used as a set/reset latch: PRE_N = START_N, CLR_N = RESET_N, CLK = GND (no clock edges), D = V3V3, Q = STARTED (TP19)",
        "START_N": "U14 gate 2: NAND(MAIN_LED_OK, RUN, V3V3, V3V3); low once U5 is on with PGOOD and FLT good, its status validated by V20_OK, while RUN. Level-sensitive, so a MAIN_OK that is already high at RESET release (PGOOD deglitch) still starts it; RUN in the gate keeps PRE_N high while RESET clears the latch",
        "TIMER_GO": "U13 gate 3 = RUN AND STARTED -> R69/R70 -> U11 SENSE (unchanged divider)",
        "ARMED": "U11 RESET output (R71 pull-up) = ARMED directly; it stays high because its input is latched",
        "ANY_BAD": "U14 gate 1 = NAND(MAIN_LED_OK, P12_OK, N12_OK, V3V3): S9.0 ties the former P5_OK input high",
